parallel-turbo.snippet:
The Abbott headquarters are located in Abbott Park, Libertyville, north of Chicago, Illinois, United States;
1888 - founded by Wallace Calvin Abbott (c. 1858-1921), who made dosimetric granules above his People's Drug Store in Chicago, United States; 1900 - company incorporated as The Abbott Alkaloidal Co. 1910 - the business expands with branches on New York, San Francisco, Seattle, Toronto, agency for Europe in London and business on India. 1915 - company name changed to Abbott Laboratories. 1937 - name changed to Abbott Laboratories Inc with UK subsiduary Abbott Laboratories (England) Ltd at 3 Wadsworth Road, Perivale, Middlesex. Manufactured as well as supplied
1946 - Abbott Laboratories Eire Ltd established to market and distribute;
